From: Robert Vokac <robertvokac@robertvokac.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] emscripten: tolerate a missing /tmp/filedrop when a window is
 destroyed

Emscripten_set_drag_event_callbacks creates /tmp/filedrop inside a try/catch,
so every window shares the directory, but Emscripten_unset_drag_event_callbacks
removes it unguarded. With two windows on one page the first destroy removes
the directory and the second destroy's FS.rmdir throws ErrnoError(ENOENT) out
of MAIN_THREAD_EM_ASM into whatever called SDL_DestroyWindow.

Not an upstream commit: SDL main still has the unguarded rmdir (checked
2026-09-30). Carried by CNA (plans/plan_bindings_upstream.md BINDFIX-052).
---
diff --git a/src/video/emscripten/SDL_emscriptenevents.c b/src/video/emscripten/SDL_emscriptenevents.c
--- a/src/video/emscripten/SDL_emscriptenevents.c
+++ b/src/video/emscripten/SDL_emscriptenevents.c
@@ -1253,7 +1253,9 @@
                 FS.rmdir(dirpath);
             }("/tmp/filedrop");
 
-            FS.rmdir("/tmp/filedrop");
+            // Every window's setup shares this one directory and ignores FS errors; teardown has to
+            // do the same, or the second window destroyed throws ENOENT out of this block.
+            try { FS.rmdir("/tmp/filedrop"); } catch (e) {}
             target.removeEventListener("dragover", SDL3.eventHandlerDropDragover);
             SDL3.eventHandlerDropDragover = undefined;
             SDL3.eventHandlerDropDrop = undefined;
